{# The page that posts a SAML message (beffroi/saml, spec/saml.md section 6.8, spec/bindings.md section 6.7, SAML
   Bindings §3.5.4): a response or a message of Single Logout to a service provider, or, when "upstream" is true, an
   AuthnRequest to the single sign-on service of an upstream identity provider (S-51), whose words say so. Its form,
   whose action and values Twig escapes for an HTML attribute, submitted by the one script below, which the
   Content-Security-Policy of the page names by its hash, never by "unsafe-inline"; a browser without scripting is shown
   the sentence and the button.
   This page does not extend the layout of the interaction plane, on purpose, as the page of the form post response
   mode does not: it carries a message of the protocol, and its policy is "default-src 'none'". Overridable by an
   application under templates/bundles/BeffroiBundle/, the script kept exactly as it is given: its hash is the policy. #}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}
{% set words = (upstream ?? false) ? 'saml_post.upstream' : 'saml_post' %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale|replace({'_': '-'}) }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ (words ~ '.title')|trans }}</title>
</head>
<body>
    <main>
        <form method="post" action="{{ action }}">
            {% for name, value in fields %}
                <input type="hidden" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ value }}">
            {% endfor %}
            <noscript>
                <p>{{ (words ~ '.explanation')|trans }}</p>
                <button type="submit">{{ 'saml_post.continue'|trans }}</button>
            </noscript>
        </form>
    </main>
    <script>{{ script|raw }}</script>
</body>
</html>
